  "notes": "Protocol 3 signs everything with hybrid Ed25519 + ML-DSA-65 and refuses v2. Every client listed implements it: Go, Python, JavaScript, the C core (OpenSSL 3.5+) and its bindings. Linux is the validated runtime. WebAssembly/WASI uses a native Python/Wasmtime host; standalone browser identity is unsupported. Wolfram 15/Linux remains a source preview: all 69 shared cases and TLS checks passed locally, while hosted CI checks only the Java/native bridge. A stable release remains gated on repeatable licensed runtime CI; see https://github.com/licensebox/wolfram/blob/main/VALIDATION.md.",
